>From porthelp:
tile_file:
An alternative file containing bitmap to use for tiles. This file should
be a .bmp and should be organized as 40 rectangular tiles wide...

bitmaps, whether bmp or xbm/xpm, have two benefits over png. 1) It is a
lot easier to program a reader for a bitmap. Trivial almost. 2) It is a
lot easier to look at the data and figure out what the picture is.

Also, nethack tiles predate png. If not by png's invention (png 1.0 in
1997ish), then by it's general usage. (tiles were introduced in or before
3.2.2 (1996))

